    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Data modelling — the entities, before the fields",
      "prov:value": "A model is wrong in a way no schema check can catch when a fact that belongs\nto one thing is written on another. That is not a style complaint. This\nrepository has paid for it repeatedly and the shape is always the same:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Data modelling — the entities, before the fields",
      "prov:value": "- `fallbackCapabilityId` said *what substitutes for `lean-toolchain`* on five\n  SKILLS. It is a fact about `lean-toolchain`. Five copies, and a change of\n  substitute could be made four times (bean `sym3`).\n- `fallbackRole` said *which role takes over* on a skill, when the BPMN\n  already said it executably. One fact, two places, nothing asserting they\n  agreed (bean `85e8`).\n- `roles:` said *who performs this skill* in 114 files, in a vocabulary that\n  resolved against nothing, for three months (bean `qif9`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean sym3",
        "bean 85e8",
        "bean qif9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "5. Say which facts are derived, and never store those",
      "prov:value": "A derived fact stored is a cache, and an unvalidated cache is worse than no\ncache. If a value can be computed from the model, computing it is the\ndeclaration — see `85e8`, where the role a process falls back to was\nrecoverable from the diagram that executes it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "6. Declare it where a tool can read it",
      "prov:value": "**And ship a reader in the same change.** Everything here that was only\ndocumentation went inert within weeks; the three examples at the top of this\npage are all of that kind. A field with no consumer is not a model, it is a\ncomment with punctuation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "7. Model VARIATION as inheritance, and earn a new kind with BEHAVIOUR",
      "prov:value": "Owner's ruling, 2026-09-20: *\"WHO should be able to override all theme\nproperties, just defaults to inherited. if it needs to name a new kind it\nshould if behaviour change.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "7. Model VARIATION as inheritance, and earn a new kind with BEHAVIOUR",
      "prov:value": "#### Worked, and it is worked because I got it wrong first"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Worked, and it is worked because I got it wrong first",
      "prov:value": "And the palette stays SHARED across all three kinds, which is the other half\nof the rule. `theme.ts` exists because 106 hardcoded hex colours became 22\nnamed properties; three kinds each with their own palette vocabulary would\nreintroduce that one level up — three spellings of \"accent colour\", free to\ndisagree about what an accent is."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "8. Point from the dependent at the general node",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-23 (#1168): *\"tasks are used to implement skills, skills\nshould not know about tasks\"* and *\"voice external to a role. should not be in\ndata model... need to flip arrows.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1168",
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "8. Point from the dependent at the general node",
      "prov:value": "**Declare which nodes are general, and let the audit hold the line.** Which\nnodes are general is a modelling decision, so it is written down: the schema\ndeclaration's doc comment carries `@general`. Today that is Role, Skill,\nRequirement statement, Graph typology, Capability, Actor and Process (#1168, B5).\n`kg:audit`'s `arrow-direction` criterion then reports two things: a `@general`\nschema whose `@ref` names a declaration that is not general, and a BPMN\n`<folio:…>` element pointing from a process at anything but a skill, role,\ndecision table, convention or precondition. It cannot see a bare string field\nwith no `@ref` (step 9 is how those become visible) or prose, so a clean run\nis a claim about declared pointers only.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1168"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "8. Point from the dependent at the general node",
      "prov:value": "**Prose may name a dependent; data may not.** The rule governs references,\nthe things a tool follows. A general node's prose can still name a\ndependent to explain itself. For example, a process's documentation may say\n\"`feature-staging.yml` publishes the branch\" so the reader knows why a step\nexists. The owner kept those explanations on 2026-09-24, since deleting them\nloses the reason a step exists (bean `epbt`). If the relation matters to a\ntool, it must also exist as data held by the dependent, like a workflow's\n`# bpmn:` line. The prose then explains that data and does not replace it.\nWhat prose cannot do is notice a rename, so `kg:audit`'s advisory\n`prose-names-resolve` criterion lists a named path whose directory exists\nand whose file does not. A bare name that nothing in the repository carries\nis left undetermined, because it could be a run's output, a folio's file or\nan example.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean epbt",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "9. Make every cross-node reference a typed KG reference",
      "prov:value": "A reference is a claim that another node exists. A bare string makes that\nclaim in a vocabulary nothing resolves: a typo, a rename or a deleted node\nreads exactly like a valid name. Owner, 2026-09-23: *\"Things like skills\nshould be KG reference.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/kg-core/data-modelling.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "9. Make every cross-node reference a typed KG reference",
      "prov:value": "**Free text stays free text** only when it is not a claim about another node:\na description, a note, a persona. `useCases` was free text that named things\nthe graph could not point at; that is the case this rule exists for, and the\nstories are now nodes that point at their role."
    }
  ]
